            "stars": 5,
            "text": "Great stuff, very easy to handle, I can strongly recommend both the gear and the dealer/manufacturer. Many thanks!",
            "author": "Joachim B.",
            "product": "120 Easyloader tray (STL)",
            "date": "August 2026",
            "source": "tonephotographic.com"
          }
        },
        "review_2": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "I have scanned six 120 rolls with the Tone 120 dslr scanning system and it is a hit with me. )I also purchased the 35mm system, and have scanned two rolls so far. I paired them with an old laptop that I installed MX Linux 25.2 and Entangle to monitor the negatives as I turn the advancement dials. I like being able to sit down to scan. Finally, I can get perfectly aligned shots, and I can fill the frame using a geared Nikon GP-2 camera focusing stage to utilize the max resolution/area of the camera by raising and lowering the dslr in a controlled fashion. This also allows instant 90 degree orientation switching when going from 4.5x6 to 6x7 or half frame 35mm to full frame. Another wonderful feature is how easy it is to start the roll - just push it in until it contacts the silicone wheels, and start turning CCW. The Tone dslr scanning system is a well thought out and engineered system.",
            "author": "James M.",
            "product": "toneCarrier 120",
            "date": "July 2026",
            "source": "tonephotographic.com"
          }
        },
        "review_3": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "Great kit and easy to use with the printed parts! It gives the assembled tonecarrier some weight and sturdiness.",
